Patch 2028: bigger shader caches without index shifting, evicted objects released only after the GPU is done with them.

The per-draw vertex shader cache held 128 entries and the guest-FP pipeline cache 256, both evicting the oldest by moving the
whole table down. A J-Stars fight needs more than that (pipelines reached 326-391 in two fights), so:
- the vertex shader eviction moved every entry down one slot under vs_idx values already recorded for this frame and stored in
  pipeline entries, so a draw could be recorded with another program's slot;
- both evictions released a shader blob or pipeline that a draw recorded earlier in the frame, or a command list still on the
  GPU, could still use;
- pipelines were rebuilt (D3DCompile and the driver compiler, 11% of the drawing thread in a fight sample).
Now: 1024 vertex shaders and 4096 pipelines; a full vertex shader cache reuses slots in turn without moving them (pipeline
entries built on a reused slot stop matching); evicted objects wait in a list and are released after render_frame has
drained the GPU two frames later; the pipeline lookup tries the last index found for the same program hash first.

Tested (US disc, Free Battle, scripted route): a fight with 326 pipelines and no eviction message; game flips per second over
150 s of the fight 15.9 (15.5 before); pictures as before. A second run was lost to the menu route. Not tested: a session long
enough to fill 4096 pipelines.

